# The claims that span a width, wherever in a document they sit. One row per claim whose low and
# high differ, so there is something a narrowing statement could actually reduce.
#
# The denominator for every question about uncertainty
#   This is the denominator for every question about uncertainty in a filing. Judging whether a
#   narrowing sentence would narrow the range is prose and belongs to a person. Counting how many
#   ranges decline to say anything at all is arithmetic, and it turns "a claim without one is
#   weaker" from an opinion into a figure.
#
# The mirror of the point rule
#   A range filing `narrowsWhen` as `notApplicable` is claiming it has no range, in a row that
#   demonstrably has one.
-- pm:Claim where low <> high, at every element that carries one.
SELECT c.*
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT c.is_a_point
